    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required that a created owner returns `displayName` formatted as `'LastName, FirstName'`. The acceptance test creates an owner via `POST /api/owners` and reads it back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`, expecting `$.displayName` to equal `\"LastName, FirstName\"`.\n\nSince `OwnerDto` is generated from `openapi.yml` at build time, I made two small, well-placed changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 mapped `displayName` via a single-responsibility helper:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\", expression = \"java(displayName(owner))\")\n   OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);\n\n   default String displayName(Owner owner) {\n       return owner.getLastName() + \", \" + owner.getFirstName();\n   }\n   ```\n\nThe formatting lives in one small method inside the mapper (the natural home for entity\u2192DTO derivation), and it's applied wherever `toOwnerDto` is used \u2014 both the create responder and the GET responder \u2014 from the stored names. Full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
